            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 72-year-old female patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she displayed significant dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemic respiratory failure, chest X-ray showing hyperinflation without consolidation, and blood tests revealing mild inflammatory markers. Spirometry confirmed severely reduced airflow. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and closely monitored with pulse oximetry and regular vital signs assessment. She responded well to treatment with clear clinical improvement. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided prior to discharge. Please arrange follow-up including pulmonary rehabilitation. Discharge medication adjustments are enclosed. Kind regards, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>
               </text>
            </section>
